body:
### Tested versions

- Reproducible in: 
  - v4.6.1-stable_mono_win64
- Not Reproducible in: 
  - v4.5.1-stable_mono_win64
  - v4.4.1-stable_mono_win64

### System information

Windows 11 - Godot v4.6.1.stable.mono.official.14d19694e - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 (nvidia, 591.74) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-10900 CPU @ 2.80GHz (2.80 GHz)

### Issue description

When calling: `MultiMeshInstance2D.Multimesh.SetInstanceColor`
Specifically later on, after the initial setup, when updating an instance from something like a physics event.

### Steps to reproduce

Create a class that inherits from `MultiMeshInstance2D`
i,e,:
`public partial class ExampleRenderer : MultiMeshInstance2D`

Some Extras:
```cs
[Export]
public Material _material;

private readonly Color WHITE = new(1f, 1f, 1f);

private readonly Color TRANSPARENT_BLACK = new(0f, 0f, 0f, 0f);

private readonly Vector2[] UVS =
    [
        Vector2.Down,   // 0, 1
        Vector2.Zero,   // 0, 0
        Vector2.Right,  // 1, 0
        Vector2.One     // 1, 1
    ];
```
Note, the material was using the custom data on a custom shader below
```shader
shader_type canvas_item;

void vertex() {
	// Called for every vertex the material is visible on.
	switch(VERTEX_ID) {
		case 0:
			UV.x = INSTANCE_CUSTOM.r;
			UV.y = INSTANCE_CUSTOM.a;
			break;
		case 1:
			UV.x = INSTANCE_CUSTOM.r;
			UV.y = INSTANCE_CUSTOM.g;
			break;
		case 2:
			UV.x = INSTANCE_CUSTOM.b;
			UV.y = INSTANCE_CUSTOM.a;
			break;
		case 3:
			UV.x = INSTANCE_CUSTOM.b;
			UV.y = INSTANCE_CUSTOM.g;
			break;
		default:
			break;
	}
}
```


In your `_Ready` function:
```cs

this.Multimesh = new MultiMesh()
{
    TransformFormat = MultiMesh.TransformFormatEnum.Transform2D,
    UseColors = true,
    InstanceCount = 0,
    UseCustomData = true,
    PhysicsInterpolationQuality = MultiMesh.PhysicsInterpolationQualityEnum.Fast
};

this.Multimesh.SetInstanceCount(2);
this.Material = this._material;
```

Setup an example surface:
```cs
// Build Mesh
var mesh = new ImmediateMesh();
mesh.SurfaceBegin(Mesh.PrimitiveType.TriangleStrip);

mesh.SurfaceSetUV(UVS[0]);
mesh.SurfaceAddVertex2D(Vector2.Zero);

mesh.SurfaceSetUV(UVS[1]);
mesh.SurfaceAddVertex2D(Vector2.Up);

mesh.SurfaceSetUV(UVS[2]);
mesh.SurfaceAddVertex2D(Vector2.Right);

mesh.SurfaceSetUV(UVS[3]);
mesh.SurfaceAddVertex2D(Vector2.One);

mesh.SurfaceEnd();
this.Multimesh.SetMesh(mesh);

this.Multimesh.SetInstanceTransform2D(
                    0,
                    new Transform2D(
                        0f,
                        Vector2.One,
                        0.0f,
                        Vector2.Zero
                    ));
this.Multimesh.SetInstanceCustomData(0, WHITE);
this.Multimesh.SetInstanceColor(0, WHITE);

this.Multimesh.SetInstanceTransform2D(
                    1,
                    new Transform2D(
                        0f,
                        Vector2.One,
                        0.0f,
                        Vector2.One
                    ));
this.Multimesh.SetInstanceCustomData(1, WHITE);
this.Multimesh.SetInstanceColor(1, WHITE);
```
In the example, I'm using all white for the `custom_data`, but in reality it's matching up with an atlas.

Then, on for example a button press, or whatever way you choose to Update the Multimesh:
```cs
this.Multimesh.SetInstanceCount(2);

this.Multimesh.SetInstanceTransform2D(
                    0,
                    new Transform2D(
                        0f,
                        Vector2.One,
                        0.0f,
                        Vector2.Zero
                    ));
this.Multimesh.SetInstanceCustomData(0, WHITE);
this.Multimesh.SetInstanceColor(0, WHITE);

this.Multimesh.SetInstanceTransform2D(
                    1,
                    new Transform2D(
                        0f,
                        Vector2.One * 2f,
                        0.0f,
                        Vector2.One * 2f
                    ));
this.Multimesh.SetInstanceCustomData(1, WHITE);
this.Multimesh.SetInstanceColor(1, TRANSPARENT_BLACK);
```

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

Okay... Nevermind... It's working on my MRP... Yet, still not working on my main project...
Please help... this is driving me absolutely insane...

